            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Giorgio and Fred ride their bicycles towards each other from points 12 km apart. Giorgio rides 2 km/h faster than Fred, and they meet in 1 hour. How fast did each of them ride?",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Giorgio: $7\\text{ km/h}$; Fred: $5\\text{ km/h}$.",
      "worked": "Let $v\\text{ km/h}$ be Fred's speed. Giorgio's speed is $(v+2)\\text{ km/h}$. After 1 hour, their distances add to 12 km.\n$$\\begin{align*}v+v+2&=12\\\\2v&=10\\\\v&=5\\end{align*}$$\nFred rides at $5\\text{ km/h}$ and Giorgio rides at $5+2=7\\text{ km/h}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
